# Data and API reference

The authoritative route inventory is `docs/agent/project-manifest.json` and the
authoritative access policy is in `firestore.rules` and `storage.rules`.

## Boundary rules

- Protected API handlers verify Firebase ID tokens or portal capabilities.
- Request bodies are schema-validated and ownership is checked server-side.
- Firestore reads are bounded and indexed; list endpoints use cursor pagination.
- Storage uploads use canonical backend paths and short-lived signed URLs.
- Real-time voting uses read-only projection documents; clients do not write
  poll results.

When adding a route or collection, update its validation, authorization,
index/rule requirements, client contract, and run `pnpm context:refresh`.
